### Storage node filling up
More than **{{ threshold }}%** of this node's Portworx pool capacity is used. Plan more capacity before it reaches 80%.

#### Check first
1. [Node metrics](/#/components/{{ componentUrnForUrl }}/metrics) → **Portworx** tab: capacity, pool usage and replica count.
2. [Portworx - Nodes and pools](/#/dashboards/urn:stackpack:portworx:dashboard:nodes): compare nodes. One full node usually means the replicas are spread unevenly.
3. `kubectl -n <portworx-namespace> exec <px-cluster-pod> -c portworx -- /opt/pwx/bin/pxctl status` and `kubectl -n <portworx-namespace> exec <px-cluster-pod> -c portworx -- /opt/pwx/bin/pxctl service pool show` on the node.

#### Fix
1. Add capacity: expand the pool (`kubectl -n <portworx-namespace> exec <px-cluster-pod> -c portworx -- /opt/pwx/bin/pxctl service pool expand`) or add drives to the StorageCluster.
2. Rebalance replicas to emptier nodes: `kubectl -n <portworx-namespace> exec <px-cluster-pod> -c portworx -- /opt/pwx/bin/pxctl service pool rebalance` (Portworx 3.x) or `volume ha-update`.
3. Delete unused volumes and old snapshots.

#### Verify
The used share drops below the threshold.
